# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tags[n].block(result) — blocks the strand under that tag with a
#         return value injected on unblock; used to implement parallel memoized Fibonacci.
# blocked: block() takes no value.  Probed: the arity guard refuses an
#          argument, so `tags[n].block(result)` -- the whole memoization
#          mechanism -- cannot be written.  List indexing and method
#          dispatch on the element both work (`l[0].stop()` probed OK), so
#          valued block is the only gap.
# matrix-row: tag-block
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture uses tags[n].block(v) — calling block() with a return value on
#   a UTag held in a List (array indexing).  This requires M4 prototype-OOP
#   dispatch, the List type, detach() builtin, and complex cross-strand
#   synchronization via tagged sleep.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with tag method dispatch and List type):
# # var tags = [] | for(var i = 0; i <= 20; i++) tags.insertBack(Tag.new()) | ...
# # detach(fibo(10))|; tags[10]: sleep();
# # [00000001] 89
